// add -- the Pyrope equivalent of verilog/add.sv.
//
// Hand-written, not emitted from the Verilog: a machine emission would enter
// the same LGraph the Verilog does and measure the two FRONT ENDS rather than
// the two languages. See [status].pyrope in design.toml.
//
// The width is spelled as a sized type rather than carried in a constant, so
// this module is monomorphic and design.toml pins the matching single config
// (BW = 8). Keeping it monomorphic also keeps the emitted netlist name stable
// across runs, which the ABC cache keys on.

// `wrap` because the sum of two 8-bit values needs 9 bits and the Verilog
// truncates. An unannotated narrowing assignment is a compile error in Pyrope,
// which makes explicit exactly the overflow the SystemVerilog performs silently.
pub comb add(a:u8, b:u8) -> (result:u8) {
  wrap result = a + b
}
